{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346173-laughing-devil-distraction-and-the-missing-charm-type","id":1346173,"title":"Laughing Devil Distraction, and the missing Charm Type","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-05T09:08:03-08:00","id":1346173,"title":"Laughing Devil Distraction, and the missing Charm Type","content":"There's an unusual type of charm with which isn't really supported by the rules. Most Charms fall under 4 categories - <br /> <br /> * Permanent (Always on)<br /> <br /> * Simple (create an action and cannot be flurried, generally used for significant enhancements/setups/transformations or finishing moves)<br /> <br /> * Supplemental (which are just used to enhance their associated Ability/Attribute) <br /> <br /> * Reflexive (which create an action at any point - usually as a way of responding to something else or to activate a power that isn't hugely scene-changing<br /> <br /> There's a missing type of Charm here - a charm which creates an action that isn't as impactful as a Simple Charm, but uses a dice pool that isn't one of the standard actions. Simple charms can't be flurried, which means they take all of a character's focus for a turn. What's missing is a charm which creates a smaller action - for example, Laughing Devil Distraction, which has raised quite a few questions. <br /> <br /> Laughing Devil Distraction lets you do a special Distract gambit that seems to be mechanically unusual. It's a Simple Charm that can be flurried<br /> <br /> Can you Flurry Laughing Devil Distraction with an attack, or does it use your attack for the turn?<br /> <br /> Since the usual dice pool for a Distract Gambit would be Dexterity + [Melee, Brawl, Martial Arts etc] can you use Dexterity charms to enhance Laughing Devil Distraction, or Manipulation charms only?<br /> <br /> Similarly, can you use Laughing Devil Distraction with Martial Arts Charms that care about distraction - such as Deeper into Trouble Technique from Laughing Monster style<br /> <br /> On top of that - has anyone written any custom charms that fall into this odd fifth category? Do they have any interesting ideas for that sort of charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6706-meetcute","name":"MeetCute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:12:52-08:00","id":1346198,"title":"","content":"Exalted is a system in which specific overrides general, but that also means that <i>absent</i> a specific rule saying otherwise, you're supposed to follow the general rule.<br /> <br /> \u200bLaughing Devil Distraction is a gambit that can be placed in a flurry; a gambit is a kind of attack; two attacks can't be placed in a flurry; thus, Laughing Devil Distraction can't be placed in a flurry with an attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:49:26-08:00","id":1346438,"title":"","content":"I think I agree with Alucard, but it's also worth acknowledging that (in the exception-based framework) it's confusing for the Charm to mention flurries, because by default that's true of ANY gambit. So why talk like you're stating an exception if no exception is being made? Which makes one wonder, are they trying to except something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:23:28-08:00","id":1346623,"title":"","content":"I'd say it cannot be improved by distract-improving martial arts or dexterity charms - it's neither a dexterity nor a martial arts roll.<br /> <br /> There are two Silver-Voiced Nightingale charms with a similar activation condition - Terrifying Battle Shriek and Haunting Heart-Rending Melody.<br /> <br /> As for home-brew, I made this charm as part of a martial art I'm working around:<br /> <br /> <b>Space-Filling Knives Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Martial Arts 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mastery, Terrestrial, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One Turn<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b>Cutting the Knot Form<br /> The martial artist assumes a defensive stance, weapons spinning such that no matter where her enemy strikes, a blade is there to snatch if from the air.<br /> Ignore onslaught penalties until your next turn. Attacks which miss you inflict 1 point of onslaught penalty on them, you may pay up to (amount they missed by) initiative to deal that many dice of hardness-ignoring damage (type is based on a weapon you wield)<br /> Terrestrial: Damage max is (essence)<br /> Mastery: You may flurry this with a defend other action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}